08000" direction="3" style="0">SCL</LABEL><LABEL pos="65.5,66" font="5" color="208000" direction="3" style="0">SDA</LABEL><POWER pos="132,80" which="0" direction="0">3V3</POWER><JUNCTION pos="153,86"/><POWER pos="140,86" which="4" direction="1">0</POWER><LABEL pos="155,89.065625" font="5" color="208000" direction="1" style="0">SCL</LABEL><LABEL pos="161,88.9296875" font="5" color="208000" direction="1" style="0">SDA</LABEL><LABEL pos="223,117.4296875" font="5" color="208000" direction="1" style="0">SDA</LABEL><LABEL pos="225,90" font="5" color="208000" direction="1" style="0">SCL</LABEL><POWER pos="245,114" which="4" direction="1">0</POWER><POWER pos="260,106" which="0" direction="0">3V3</POWER><NOTE_TEXT a="20,128" b="145,166" font="5" color="453626" style="4" fill="0" direction="3" border_style="2">Matching SDA / SCL labels form the I2C bus.GPIO21 = SDA; GPIO22 = SCL.ENV1 SDO is grounded: address 0x76.USB powers U1; both modules use its 3V3 rail.</NOTE_TEXT><NOTE_TEXT a="20,183" b="280,201" font="5" color="453626" style="4" fill="0" direction="3" border_style="2">PCB wiring example. Spare headers, ENV1 3Vo and CS are open intentionally.Configure the OLED address and firmware for the named boards. See Explanation for the full pin table.</NOTE_TEXT></TinyCAD><DSNSETTINGS><SHOW_RULERS>1</SHOW_RULERS></DSNSETTINGS><NETLIST_TYPES><TYPE name="default"/></NETLIST_TYPES></TinyCADSheets>